  "manual_actual_callflow": {
    "send": "Default/command/channel/provider/twoSE4/twoSPI guards2864..28bc; claim LSE28d4 or LL/SC2c34..2c48. Submit printk2c80 then STLR owner2c8c then original writel28ec; wait2918. Success-close2ac0 then printk2ae0; timeout original read2988 then close2af4/print2b14. Event command cmp/branch2994/2998 or2b18/2b1c avoids channel dereference299c and reaches EIO2b70. No success manufactured.",
    "globalIRQ": "Original read8a80, acquire owner8aa4, original clear8ab0; original error read8ad0/clear8ae4 retained, pointer compare8ae8 then one-shot. Invalid IRQ format has separate path8c18..9244 using the same once variable. Original callback remains KCFI checked8bf0..8c08.",
    "EVIRQ": "Acquire eligibility8cec before original read8d30,clear8d44,contextread8d4c; raw context kept w21 at8d5c, masked/adjusted state w25 stored8d6c. Original complete_all8dc0 then captured-pointer compare8dc4, single-claim log911c. No reloading owner after completion, so allowed late output preserved.",
    "atomic_alternatives": "Both compiled LSE CASAL and LL/SC retry alternatives inspected; retry loops are standard kernel atomic implementation, not bounded-time scheduling proof.",
    "disabled": "BSS bool0 makes begin skip all metadata filters/claim/submit; owner staysNULL and IRQ one-shot/log blocks skipped. Extra software loads/branches remain; no claim of instruction-byte identity with baseline."
  },
